  "Question": "Calculate: \\(314\\times3\\times3\\times6\\div3\\div100=?\\) (Answer as a decimal.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "56.52",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Multiplication and division by the same nonzero number undo each other, so one factor of \\(3\\) cancels the division by \\(3\\). Regrouping the remaining factors gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n314\\times3\\times3\\times6\\div3\\div100\n&=314\\times(3\\times6)\\div100\\\\\n&=314\\times18\\div100\\\\\n&=5652\\div100.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nDividing by \\(100\\) moves the decimal point two places to the left, so the answer is \\(56.52\\).",
